\b\fs36\cf1 Common Toolbar
\par \pard \plain\fs24 If a \uldb \b User profile\plain\b\fs24 {\v V_JNBJ@admin32.hlp}\plain\fs24  is configured by the \uldb \b Administrator\plain\b\fs24 {\v Contents@admin32.hlp}\plain\fs24  with the attribute \b Use Common Toolbar \plain\fs24 then thistoolbar is always loaded from\b  ...\'5cLEO\'5cLEO32\'5cUSER\'5cCOMMON.UTB\plain\fs24  and the user is prohibited from changing the current toolbar.
\par 
\par The enables the Supervisor to set up a group of users with a common (and possibly restricted function) toolbar.
\par 
\par \uldb \b How to set up a common toolbar\plain\b\fs24 {\v WKOUPN@how_to.hlp}\plain\fs24 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Contents of Toolbar Editor}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Contents}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Contents of Toolbar Editor
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Select \b Edit\plain\fs24  then \{bmc bm0.bmp\} point to \b Toolbar\plain\fs24  and \ul click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} with the left mouse button to open the Toolbar Editor.
\par 
\par This editor window provides facilities generate your specific \uldb \b Tool Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v 1Y24MM@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24  and save it to disk or load a previously saved Tool Bar from disk.
\par You may also \uldb \b define your own Bitmaps\plain\b\fs24 {\v Define_your_own_Bitmaps}\plain\fs24  for icons.
\par The \b Tool Customise Window\plain\fs24  has three tabs to select the \ul icons\plain\fs24 {\v ICON@Sem.HLP} and the functions for the icons:
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \{bmc bm6.bmp\}
\par 
\par \tab \uldb \b User Toolbar\plain\b\fs24 {\v User_Toolbar}\tab \plain\fs24 Adds or removes icons, saves and loads Tool Bars.
\par \b 
\par \tab \uldb Left Mouse Click Button Assignments\plain\b\fs24 {\v Left_Mouse_Click_Button_Assignments}\tab \tab \plain\fs24 Assigns actions to the left mouse button.
\par \b 
\par \tab \uldb Middle Mouse Click Button Assignments\plain\b\fs24 {\v Middle_Mouse_Click_Button_Assignments}\tab \plain\fs24 Assigns actions to the middle mouse button.
\par \b 
\par \plain\fs24 There are four buttons common for the tabs:\tab \{bmc bm7.bmp\}
\par 
\par \b \tab OK\tab \plain\fs24 \tab Closes the editor and saves changes if any. (Will be greyed if User is configured to use a \uldb \b Common Toolbar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Common_Toolbar}\plain\fs24 )
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \b \tab Cancel\tab \plain\fs24 Closes the editor and disregards any changes, same as clicking on \{bmc bm8.bmp\}.
\par 
\par \b \tab Apply\tab \tab \plain\fs24 Not used in this application, remains greyed.
\par \b 
\par \tab Help\tab \tab \plain\fs24 Displays the help for the selected tab.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Left Mouse Click Button Assignments}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Left_Mouse_Click_Button_Assignments}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Left Mouse Click Button Assignments
\par \pard \plain\fs24    
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx4535\cellx13815\pard\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\} \ul Click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on the \b Left Mouse Click Button Assignments\plain\fs24   tab.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl An action is assigned when a button of the Tool Bar is clicked with the left mouse button and also the function of the middle mouse button under this condition.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm9.bmp\} The left window shows the \uldb \b User Toolbar Buttons\plain\b\fs24 {\v User_Toolbar_Buttons}\plain\fs24  (\ul icons\plain\fs24 {\v ICON@Sem.HLP}) and their definitions which are in use.
\par\intbl \{bmc bm9.bmp\} The middle window shows the assignment tree of the \uldb \b Select Button Action\plain\b\fs24 {\v Select_Button_Action}. \plain\fs24 It is greyed if the selection is not available.
\par\intbl \{bmc bm9.bmp\} The right window shows the assignment tree of the \uldb \b Middle Mouse Button Adjustment\plain\b\fs24 {\v Middle_Mouse_Button_Adjustment}. \plain\fs24 It is greyed if the selection is not available.
\par\intbl \{bmc bm9.bmp\} The \ul Tool Tip\plain\fs24 {\v IJYVH3@Sem.HLP} window allows to set the  \uldb \b Tool Tip Text\plain\b\fs24 {\v Tool_Tip_Text}\plain\fs24  for the selected Tool Bar button.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \ul Scroll Bars\plain\fs24 {\v 2HOSDE@Sem.HLP} allow to shift the information in the windows.\cell\pard \pard\intbl \{bmc bm10.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
\par \page
