\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx9915\cellx10415\cellx14315\pard\intbl The Middle Mouse Button Adjustment defines the secondary action when the left mouse button is clicked on the \ul icon\plain\fs24 {\v ICON@Sem.HLP}.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl The choice is:\par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm9.bmp\}\tab \b Mouse\plain\fs24 :This offers a list of parameters which may be assigned to the middle mouse adjustment pane in the User Interface Status Bar.  See \uldb \b Status Bar Parameter Control\plain\b\fs24 {\v T3KQVM@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24 . It defines what the middle mouse adjustment pane is set to.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm9.bmp\}\tab \b None\plain\fs24 :  No action.\cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl \cell\pard \pard\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm12.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 The box below the tree is a search box. Type the parameter to search for and the tree will open to that parameter.
