{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Select Button Action}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Select_Button_Action}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Left Mouse Click Button Assignments}
\b\fs36\cf1 Select Button Action
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\} \ul Click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on the \b Left Mouse Click Button Assignments\plain\fs24   tab or \b Middle Mouse Click Assignment\plain\fs24  to make the Select Button Action accessible.
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx9915\cellx10415\cellx14315\pard\intbl The Select Button Action tree defines the primary action when the left mouse button is clicked on the \ul icon\plain\fs24 {\v ICON@Sem.HLP}. 
\par\intbl The choice is:\par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm9.bmp\}\tab \b Commands\plain\fs24 : This expands to a list of possible commands for selection.
\par\intbl \{bmc bm9.bmp\}\tab \b Dialogs\plain\fs24 : This expands to give a list of possible dialogs and the tabs on the SEM Control Panel.
\par\intbl \{bmc bm9.bmp\}\tab \b Macros\plain\fs24 : This expands to show the macros available in the current macro library.
\par\intbl \{bmc bm9.bmp\}\tab \b Mouse\plain\fs24 :This offers a list of parameters which may be assigned to the left mouse adjustment pane in the User Interface Status Bar.  See \uldb \b Status Bar Parameter Control\plain\b\fs24 {\v T3KQVM@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24 . If one of these parameters is selected it enables the \uldb \b Middle Mouse Button Adjustment\plain\b\fs24 {\v Middle_Mouse_Button_Adjustment}\plain\fs24  tree which defines what the middle mouse adjustment pane is set to as part of the same action.
\par\intbl \{bmc bm9.bmp\}\tab \b None\plain\fs24 :  No action.\cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl \cell\pard \pard\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm15.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm9.bmp\}\tab \b Parameters\plain\fs24 : This allows selection of any read/write parameter. The action is the same as a click on the parameter in the status window. If the parameter is entry only a dialog box is displayed permitting the value to be typed in. If the parameter is mouse adjustable then it is selected to the left mouse adjustment pane in the status bar. See \b Status Bar Parameter Control\plain\fs24 .
\par \{bmc bm9.bmp\}\tab \b Special Functions\plain\fs24 : These are used where a function cannot be achieved by a macro (e.g. Save System Conditions).
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm9.bmp\}\tab \b Toggle\plain\fs24 : This offers a choice of binary state digital parameters and cause the icon to toggle (e.g. Focus Wobble On /Off).
\par 
\par \pard\tx355 The box below the tree is a search box. Type the parameter to search for and the tree will open to that parameter.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 The current selection path is displayed above the tree window (e.g. Mouse).
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b Left Mouse Click Button Assignment\plain\fs24  tab and \b Middle Mouse Click Assignment\plain\fs24  tab use the same Select Button Action tree except for the toggle function.
\par \page
