\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx7935\cellx8435\cellx11525\pard\intbl\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\} Select the button \ul \b\ul icon\plain\b\fs24 {\v ICON@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24  you want to edit. 
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \ul Scroll Bars\plain\fs24 {\v 2HOSDE@Sem.HLP} allow to shift the information in the window.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm18.bmp\}\tab A button must not be locked in order to edit its characteristics.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm20.bmp\}\tab \b A locked icon is signified by a red mesh overlay\plain\fs24 . \b Locked icons apply across all Tool Bars.\plain\fs24 
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl If the icon is locked, click on \b Unlocked\plain\fs24 .
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm16.bmp\}  An icon function may be predefined and locked or unlocked if the user has the \b Unlock Tool Bar Icon\plain\fs24  privilege. In this case the User Toolbar Button field includes a pair of Locked / Unlocked buttons 
\par\intbl 
