{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Define your own Bitmaps}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Define_your_own_Bitmaps}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Define your own Bitmaps
\par \pard \plain\fs24 Each of the bitmap images provided as standard has a number in the range 1 through 52
\par Example: Icon 1 is the restore Icon \{bmc bm22.bmp\} 
\par To determine the icon numbers in your current toolbar select context help mode \b <Shift + F1> \plain\fs24 and then click on an icon.
\par 
\par When a toolbar is loaded (on User Interface Start or load/edit in the toolbar editor) the software searches for an icon file and, if it finds it, loads it in place of the standard icon bitmap. (Note, once a replacement bitmap is loaded it will only revert to the standard on restarting the UIF after the file(s) have been deleted).
\par \pard 
\par If the \uldb common Toolbar\plain\fs24 {\v Common_Toolbar} property is not set for the user the search locations are:
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 1.\tab In the \b user directory\plain\fs24 
\par 2.\tab In the Distribution directory (\b ..\'5cleo32\'5cdistrib\plain\fs24 )
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 If the common toolbar property is set the search location is:
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \f3 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\f1 \tab \b ..\'5cleo32\'5cuser\plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 The bitmaps will be used even if a common toolbar is not present\b 
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 Toolbar Icon Files have a standard name format which is \b TOOLn.BMP\plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \b 
\par \pard\tx355 To Create an Icon Bitmap file:
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs24 Use MS Paint (\b Start-programs-accessories-paint\plain\fs24 )\b 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs24 Set the Image attributes to 32 pixels wide and 31 pixels high
\par \pard\tx355 \b \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs24 Tip - use \b View-zoom-large size\plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \b \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs24 Design your bitmap\b 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs24 SaveAs \b TOOLn.BMP\plain\fs24  and must be 16 colour bitmap format
